                            Your initial purchase includes <strong>1 full year of standard updates and support</strong> absolutely free. After the first year expires, you can optionally pay a renewal fee of $40 to extend your access to new updates and support for another year.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- FAQ: runtime engines -->
                <div class="mb-2 border-0 card rounded">
                    <div id="headingEngine">
                        <button class="text-left shadow-none btn-lg btn btn-dark btn-block collapsed" type="button" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#collapseEngine" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseEngine">
                            <i class="fas fa-server mr-2"></i> Do I need Swoole or RoadRunner to run GDPlayer?
                        </button>
                    </div>
                    <div id="collapseEngine" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="headingEngine" data-parent="#accGDPlayer">
                        <div class="card-body text-muted">
                            No. GDPlayer runs on standard PHP-FPM out of the box. Swoole and RoadRunner are optional long-running engines that remove per-request bootstrap overhead for high-traffic sites. The core ships a worker-safe pipeline (PSR-7, no superglobals, no exit/die) so either engine can be adopted without patching the codebase. Engines are licensed separately, or bundled in the <strong>Runtime Bundle</strong>. In our own load test (100 simultaneous visitors on the homepage, 80 seconds, same server) the runtime ended with 0 failed requests and an average response of 21&nbsp;ms, against 164&nbsp;ms on nginx and 273&nbsp;ms on Apache.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- FAQ: pricing -->
                <div class="mb-2 border-0 card rounded">
                    <div id="headingPrice">
                        <button class="text-left shadow-none btn-lg btn btn-dark btn-block collapsed" type="button" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#collapsePrice" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapsePrice">
                            <i class="fas fa-tag mr-2"></i> Why did the license price change?
                        </button>
                    </div>
                    <div id="collapsePrice" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="headingPrice" data-parent="#accGDPlayer">
                        <div class="card-body text-muted">
                            The Single License is now <strong>$149</strong> (previously $99) because the core was rebuilt around a worker-safe, long-running-ready pipeline plus native Swoole and RoadRunner support. Licenses purchased before the change keep their existing terms and the same <strong>$40/year</strong> renewal fee.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- FAQ 5 -->
                <div class="mb-2 border-0 card rounded">
                    <div id="heading5">
                        <button class="text-left shadow-none btn-lg btn btn-dark btn-block collapsed" type="button" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#collapse5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse5">
                            <i class="fas fa-shield-alt mr-2"></i> Is there any warranty or guarantee?
                        </button>
                    </div>
                    <div id="collapse5" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="heading5" data-parent="#accGDPlayer">
                        <div class="card-body text-muted">
                            We guarantee the script functions exactly as advertised on supported server environments. If a bug arises from the script itself, we will provide patches via updates. Please note that misconfigured servers can cause errors, which is why we highly recommend our installation support.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- FAQ 6 (REFUND POLICY FIXED) -->
                <div class="mb-2 border-0 card rounded">
                    <div id="heading6">
                        <button class="text-left shadow-none btn-lg btn btn-danger btn-block collapsed" type="button" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#collapse6" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse6">
